{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\nThe completion verifier's step budget routinely exhausts on legitimate validation work, failing criteria as \"unmet\" that are merely unproven-within-budget (fb8a: request_limit=24, 2 false unmets; the pony epic: repeated exhaustion, 5 then 1 false unmets). The pressure drives operators toward attestation-laundering.\n\n## Design intent (operator-stated, canonical)\nThe budget's ONLY goal is preventing runaway tool use. For valid tool use the floor must be GENEROUS with ample scaling; we never artificially limit authorized validation.\n\n## Current mechanics\n`verify_step_floor(c) = clamp(steps_per_criterion x c, step_floor_min, 480)`, defaults 8/48; structured_run halves steps into request_limit (6-AC epic: 48 steps = 24 requests). Defects: (1) story-calibrated cost model — epic criteria traverse child tickets (show_ticket + comments + repo reads, 5-10 requests each) plus fixed overhead, no evidence-surface term; (2) runaway is ALREADY separately guarded (tool_calls_limit, loop/repeat detection, the clamp), so a small budget adds no safety, only false FAILs; (3) no cross-run carryover — every re-verify re-proves all criteria (whack-a-mole, ~10 min/cycle).\n\n## Plan\n1. Raise defaults: completion_verify_steps_per_criterion 8 -> 24, completion_verify_step_floor_min 48 -> 160 (supersedes the interim operator-machine config mitigation). Raise the 480 clamp to 960 so 24/criterion scales past 20 ACs — the clamp is a runaway ceiling, not a validation cap.\n2. Evidence-surface-aware scaling: budget = per_criterion x c + child_traversal x direct_children + fixed_overhead, with defaults child_traversal = 16 steps/direct child and fixed_overhead = 16 steps — grounded in the observed 5-10 REQUESTS/child (= 10-20 steps under the steps=2xrequests halving; 16 is mid-band, and the fixed initial show_ticket + description parse sizes the same). Both are new config keys (completion_verify_child_traversal_steps, completion_verify_fixed_overhead_steps) validated in _config_sections.py alongside the existing verify keys. Children counted from the ticket graph at budget-sizing time (where criteria_count is computed). The child term lands INSIDE `verify_step_floor` itself (new `direct_children: int = 0` param), NOT at the completion.py:742 call — verify_step_floor has exactly two consumers (Serena+grep verified): primary sizing (completion.py:742) and `plan_recovery_pool` (completion_banking.py:224), and the shared function keeps both on one formula (no primary/recovery divergence). `plan_recovery_pool` gains a pass-through `direct_children` param (default 0) forwarded by its sole caller (completion_recovery.py:625); its docstring oracle pins (c=8 -> floor 64, N 32, global 48, successor 16; clamp-max pins) update to the 24/160/960 mechanics with childless + childful rows.\n3. Cross-run PASS-verdict cache — a NEW ticket-scoped store; the run-scoped `CriterionBank` (completion_banking.py:396-435) stays EXACTLY as designed (run-unique dir = concurrent-close isolation, preserved). New cache at `.rebar/cache/completion_verdicts/<ticket>/<criterion-hash>.json`, written ONLY on a validated PASS at finalize (atomic tmp+rename; last-write-wins safe — entries are validated-PASS-only, keyed by content). Invalidation granularity: NOT the whole-repo HEAD tree sha (`_resolve_tree_sha` :358-373 — any unrelated commit rotates it); key each entry by (criterion-text hash, scoped material fingerprint) where the scoped fingerprint reuses `BankStamps`/`resolve_bank_stamps` (:358-392) narrowed to blobs under the ticket's file_impact paths; when own file_impact is empty but the ticket has children (the epic case — the highest-value reuse target), the fingerprint is the union of direct-child file_impact blobs: enumerate DIRECT children from the ticket graph (the same list budget sizing uses), collect each child's file_impact paths, resolve to blob shas through `BankStamps`/`resolve_bank_stamps` via a new small helper — NOT `_subtree_impacts` (completion_prefetch.py:257), which is unsuitable as-is (BFS-walks the ENTIRE subtree, returns {path: count} frequencies not blobs, excludes the root's file_impact). Whole-tree sha is the fallback ONLY for childless tickets with empty file_impact. Credit-vs-evaluate protocol: cache entries store the FULL banked record (met, evidence text, citations) from the original validated PASS; at run start (completion_recovery.py:487 `CriterionBank.for_run`) still-valid entries are SEEDED into the run's CriterionBank, each stamped with a NEW `seeded: true` flag. Seeded ids are EXCLUDED from the primary's work surface: `primary_criteria_manifest` (completion_recovery.py:540) omits already-banked criterion ids, so the primary run — launched first (:495) — is instructed only on unproven criteria (successor scoping already targets the remainder); this makes 'spend budget only on unproven criteria' hold on the PRIMARY run, not just successors. Finalizer interaction — corrected from the prior draft: `merge_finalizer_with_bank` today PRESERVES the finalizer's own met on echoed records (docstring: keeps 'a cross-criterion downgrade of a banked met=true'; only the evidence_sufficient marker is re-stamped via `_restamp_marker`), so this plan SCOPES A CHANGE to it: records flagged `seeded: true` bypass finalizer judgment — an echo of a seeded record (incl. a met:false downgrade) is replaced by the bank's validated-PASS record, and an omitted seeded record is appended from the bank. Preservation of finalizer met-downgrades for SAME-RUN (non-seeded) records is unchanged — the rule keys strictly on the seeded flag. RED test: an echo that drops OR downgrades a seeded criterion still yields the credited verdict, while a same-run record's downgrade is still preserved. Exhaustion then converges across runs. (Marker semantics from 1d71-a76c-04f6-4642 apply: cached entries are PASS-only; insufficiency is never cached.)\n4. Runaway guards stay authoritative: tool_calls_limit + loop detection unchanged; document at verify_step_floor that the budget exists ONLY for runaway prevention.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Defaults raised (24 / 160; clamp 960) with the rationale documented at verify_step_floor; a 6-AC epic sizes to >=80 requests and a 15-AC epic to >=180; unit tests on the formula, INCLUDING updating the hard-coded pins in tests/interfaces/contracts/test_completion_budget.py (verify_step_floor(1)==48, (8)==64, (40)==320, (100)==480, captured max_iterations==48, and the _VERIFY_STEP_FLOOR_MAX==480 pin) to the new 24/160/960 mechanics.\n- [ ] Budget sizing adds a child-traversal term inside verify_step_floor (new direct_children param, default 0) so BOTH consumers — completion.py:742 primary sizing and plan_recovery_pool (completion_banking.py:224, forwarded by completion_recovery.py:625) — share the formula; epic-fixture test (childful sizes strictly larger than childless at equal criteria count, for primary AND recovery pool); plan_recovery_pool docstring pins AND the hard-coded pins in tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_banking.py:53-67 (floor/N/global/successor) updated to the new mechanics plus a childful row.\n- [ ] A re-verify after exhaustion credits still-valid cached PASS verdicts (same scoped fingerprint + criterion text) by seeding them into the run-scoped CriterionBank with the seeded flag; the primary criterion-id manifest omits seeded ids (tested: seeded criteria never appear in it); the merge path credits seeded records verbatim (finalizer echo/omission cannot downgrade them) while same-run finalizer downgrades stay preserved; invalidation on fingerprint or text change is RED->GREEN; an unrelated commit outside file_impact does NOT invalidate; run-scoped bank concurrent-close isolation regression-tested.\n- [ ] Runaway protection regression-guarded: tool_calls_limit and loop detection unchanged (existing tests pass); a looping-tool fixture still trips the backstop under the larger budget.\n- [ ] `make lint`/`make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786745025428115001,"uuid":"3cd6464a-b827-4fc8-88d3-f9e0c9d76f57"}